{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":257,"aggregated":"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\n---trying POST with no body---\nerror code: 1101\nHTTP: 500","cwd":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1779028475083},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The POST with empty body still gives error 1101. But the GET with query params at least returns the platform name (even if that's not a confirmation of sending).\n\nSince the POST endpoint seems to be broken (returning 500), I should report this to the user. Let me do a final comprehensive check to see if maybe there's something I'm missing about the send mechanism.\n\nActually, looking more carefully at my earlier successful history calls - those used the `Authorization: Bearer` header. But for send, maybe I need to use a different header. Let me try `Authorization: Bearer` instead of `X-API-Key`.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-3228c0fd-566a-4d78-a8e3-0226725aa0ef","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try with Authorization header instead of X-API-Key\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer <redacted>\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"[Heartbeat 14:30 UTC]\"}' -w \"\\nHTTP: %{http_code}\"\necho \"\"\n# Also try with full auth header format\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: ApiKey echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"[Heartbeat 14:30 UTC]\"}' -w \"\\nHTTP: %{http_code}\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":670,"output":342,"cacheRead":27040,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":28052,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},